requests.txt — the request codex-cli 0.153.4 made against a gateway at
`base_url = "http://127.0.0.1:<port>/codex/v1"`, recorded 2026-09-21 for one
`codex exec` turn with a provider block using `env_key` and
`wire_api = "responses"`.

One turn produces exactly one `POST /codex/v1/responses`; the client asks for
no model list and probes no other endpoint (it only refreshes models for a
ChatGPT-backend or command-auth provider).

Headers present: originator, user-agent, session-id, thread-id,
x-client-request-id, x-codex-window-id, x-codex-beta-features,
x-codex-turn-metadata, plus accept / authorization / content-type. Absent on a
plain turn and therefore unrecorded: x-codex-installation-id,
x-codex-parent-thread-id, x-openai-subagent, x-codex-turn-state — the first
rides inside the body's `client_metadata` here, the last three only ship for
sub-agent and resumed turns.

`instructions`, `input`, `tools` and `client_metadata` values are elided: they
are the client's system prompt and the recording machine's paths, neither of
which is part of the contract. Field names, ordering and the small scalar
values are verbatim. The bearer token was a dummy; the installation id is
redacted.

Refresh this when a client release changes the contract; the profile edits
follow the fixture, never the other way round.
